BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Paws for Tales
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T180000
DTSTAMP:20260703T223108Z
UID:smcl-69fd0f2117731928001837d7@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a reluctant reader? Sign your child up for a sessi
 on to practice reading with a therapy dog at the library.\n\nStudies show 
 that children who may not want to read in front of their peers are much le
 ss anxious with an animal present. Children don't perceive animals as judg
 mental\, and reading to an animal helps them become more confident readers
 . We’d like to thank our partners for making this possible: Pet Assisted
  Therapy teams and their handlers from the Peninsula Humane Society & the 
 SPCA's Paws for Tales program.\n\nSpace is limited\, so register early for
  your 10-minute slot at smcl.org/pawsfortales! We do our best to incorpora
 te drop-ins as much as possible\, so feel free to stop by!\n\nAges: 6-11\n
 Registration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/69fd0f21
 17731928001837d7\nLast synced: 2026-07-03 15:31 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/69fd0f2117731928001837d7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[B] Baby Bounce with Stay and Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T113000
DTSTAMP:20260703T223108Z
UID:smcl-6a3b0eb3414ef43d0097de6a@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Baby storytime centers around parent/caregiver-child interacti
 ons. This storytime is developmentally appropriate for newborns and babies
  up to 18 months old. Join us for rhymes\, lap bounces\, singing\, instrum
 ents and a book or two. Stay after storytime to socialize and play.\n\nAge
 s: 0-5\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/
 6a3b0eb3414ef43d0097de6a\nLast synced: 2026-07-03 15:31 PDT
LOCATION:Belmont
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a3b0eb3414ef43d0097de6a
END:VEVENT
