BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[B] The Great Library Book Adventure With Ricky Roo & Friends
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T154500
DTSTAMP:20260703T223108Z
UID:smcl-6a19ff22a99bdd027d43456c@local-events
DESCRIPTION:When the mischievous pirate Captain Bluebeard sneaks into the 
 library and steals a book to take back to his island\, the whole library i
 s in trouble! Luckily\, a brave child from the audience steps up to the ch
 allenge. Together with Ricky Roo and his puppet friends\, they set off on 
 a silly adventure to get the book back and teach the pirate an important l
 esson: library books are meant to be shared—checked out\, enjoyed\, and 
 returned—for the whole community.\n \nA laugh-out-loud puppet show fille
 d with jokes\, audience participation\, and a heartwarming message about b
 ooks\, libraries\, and community. Perfect for young readers and future lib
 rary lovers!\n\nAges: 0-5\, 6-11\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl
 .bibliocommons.com/events/6a19ff22a99bdd027d43456c\nLast synced: 2026-07-0
 3 15:31 PDT
LOCATION:Belmont
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a19ff22a99bdd027d43456c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[B] Magic Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T163000
DTSTAMP:20260703T223108Z
UID:smcl-6a1a00eea99bdd027d4345f0@local-events
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is a crash course in the art of magic! Joe Culpe
 pper* will share secret sleight-of-hand techniques and tools for creating 
 magic effects. You will learn how to make objects magically appear\, trans
 form\, and vanish. Most important of all\, you will learn how to think and
  direct attention like a magician. No previous magic experience necessary.
  Registration is required. For children ages 8 and up.\n\n\n*Dr. Joe Cul
 pepper is a magician\, magic consultant\, and the co-editor-in-chief of th
 e academic journal Circus: Arts\, Life and Sciences. He is a former Mitacs
  Elevate postdoctoral fellow at Cirque du Soleil’s C:Lab and Concordia U
 niversity. Joe has taught magic and its adaptation to the circus arts at M
 ontreal’s National Circus School\, the Centre National des Arts du Cirqu
 e in Châlons-en-champagne\, the Lido in Toulouse\, UC Davis in California
  and beyond. He is a member of London’s Magic Circle and consults for a 
 variety of private and public organizations.\n\nAges: 6-11\, 12-18\nRegist
 ration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a1a00eea9
 9bdd027d4345f0\nLast synced: 2026-07-03 15:31 PDT
LOCATION:Belmont
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a1a00eea99bdd027d4345f0
END:VEVENT
